\f1\b0  It\'92s not technically into a Computer Use genre, but still mentioning this because it has the voice command approach.\uc0\u8232 Their marketing promises are like it\'92s Ironman\'92s JARVIS, as you can talk and it can perform task. But, they do automation based on only MCPs, and APIs. So that means, VoiceOS will only work on some specific apps based on what the app are permit to do, like general and direct stuffs like replying mails, sending messages, the obvious stuff where Ironman\'92s JARVIS should be independent to do whatever obstacles comes in front of it like a human. But, VoiceOS\'92s automation is predefined, not dynamic. I am not comparing its voice with Meridius because that\'92s now how they are build to perform action. In their usability, they are good to go. Although Meridius\'92s voice mode is more consistent over time with a Supermemory layer like Ironman\'92s JARVIS: always aware and active with the context.\
